      "writtenOn": "2023-07-19T21:01:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The current implementation exports flags referenced by _this target only_ and any flags that it receives via transitive **static** dependencies.\n\nSo basically if library A sets `export_proguard_flags_files: true` and it ends up in the transitive closure of a reverse dep (say C -static_libs-\u003e B -libs-\u003e A -static_libs-\u003e X), then C will get flags files from B, A, and X.\n\nIf B sets `export_proguard_flags_files: false` (the default), and we have this dep structure (C -libs-\u003e B -libs-\u003e A -static_libs-\u003e X), then C will get flags files from _only_ A and X.\n\n----\n\nI was going back and forth on the right semantics for this a few times. Does this make sense to you?\n\nBasically to rephrase, if a lib sets `export_proguard_flags_files: true` its flags files will end up getting referenced for every rdep above it regardless of the \"linking\" strategy (i.e. this is a really broad effect).",
      "parentUuid": "267cc351_39964746",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 76,
        "startChar": 28,
        "endLine": 76,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "80cabe0767febead4c072bf5be2bb28de2e9c054",
